---
import BlogArticle from '../../components/BlogArticle.astro';
import BlogCode from '../../components/BlogCode.astro';

const contents = [
  { id: 'scene', label: 'The message that keeps coming back' },
  { id: 'sandbox', label: 'Give the incident its own runtime' },
  { id: 'replay', label: 'Replay the payload' },
  { id: 'fix', label: 'Fix it and prove it' },
  { id: 'regression', label: 'Keep the replay as a test' },
];
const incidentSeed = `services:
  pubsub:
    topics:
      - name: orders-inbound
        subscriptions:
          - name: orders-worker-sub
  bigquery:
    datasets:
      - name: billing
    tables:
      - dataset: billing
        name: invoices
        schema:
          fields:
            - name: invoice_id
              type: STRING
              mode: REQUIRED
            - name: amount_cents
              type: INTEGER`;
const startCmd = String.raw`localcloud start --local-only --data-volume rca-incident-412 --accept-dynamic-ports
eval "$(localcloud env --data-volume rca-incident-412)"

curl -fsS -X POST "$LOCALCLOUD_GATEWAY/seed" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/yaml' \
  --data-binary @incident-seed.yaml`;
const replayPy = `import os
from google.auth.credentials import AnonymousCredentials
from google.cloud import bigquery, pubsub_v1

project = os.environ["GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT"]
publisher = pubsub_v1.PublisherClient()
subscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient()
bq = bigquery.Client(
    project=project,
    credentials=AnonymousCredentials(),
    client_options={"api_endpoint": os.environ["BIGQUERY_EMULATOR_HOST"]},
)

# The payload shape from the incident, with synthetic values.
topic = publisher.topic_path(project, "orders-inbound")
publisher.publish(topic, b"{}", invoice_id="inv-412", amount="12.50").result(timeout=30)

subscription = subscriber.subscription_path(project, "orders-worker-sub")
response = subscriber.pull(request={"subscription": subscription, "max_messages": 1}, timeout=30)
for received in response.received_messages:
    attrs = received.message.attributes
    row = {"invoice_id": attrs["invoice_id"], "amount_cents": int(attrs["amount"])}
    errors = bq.insert_rows_json(f"{project}.billing.invoices", [row])
    assert not errors, errors
    subscriber.acknowledge(request={"subscription": subscription, "ack_ids": [received.ack_id]})
    print("inserted", row)`;
const failure = `Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "replay.py", line 22, in <module>
    row = {"invoice_id": attrs["invoice_id"], "amount_cents": int(attrs["amount"])}
                                                              ~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: '12.50'`;
const fixPy = `from decimal import Decimal

row = {"invoice_id": attrs["invoice_id"], "amount_cents": round(Decimal(attrs["amount"]) * 100)}`;
const fixed = `inserted {'invoice_id': 'inv-412', 'amount_cents': 1250}`;
---

<BlogArticle
  slug="reproduce-gcp-incidents-locally"
  kind="Walkthrough"
  deck="A worker in production is choking on one message, and staging is the wrong place to poke at it. Rebuild the topic, the table and the payload on your laptop, watch it fail, and fix it with the failure in front of you."
  primary={{ href: '/docs/seed-data/', label: 'Seed data guide' }}
  secondary={{ href: '/docs/', label: 'Quick start' }}
  {contents}
  outcome="The production failure reproduced on localhost with a real traceback, a fix you watched pass, and a script you can keep as a regression test."
  needs="Python with google-cloud-pubsub and google-cloud-bigquery"
  next={{ posts: ['step-through-breakpoints-gcp', 'parallel-git-worktrees-localcloud'], doc: { href: '/docs/seed-data/', label: 'Seed data reference: every service that accepts fixtures' } }}
>
  <section>
    <h2 id="scene">The message that keeps coming back</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">The alert says the invoice worker is restarting. The logs show the same message ID again and again: the worker pulls it, crashes before acknowledging it, and Pub/Sub hands it straight back. Every other invoice is queueing behind it.</p>
    <p class="mt-4">You can't replay that payload in production, and reproducing it in shared staging means breaking the queue for everyone else. A mocked client won't help either, because the bug lives in what the real client hands your code: attributes arrive as strings, and one of them isn't the string the worker expected.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="sandbox">Give the incident its own runtime</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">Start a LocalCloud runtime on its own data volume so nothing you do here touches your everyday environment. Then describe the two resources the worker depends on, the topic with its subscription and the destination table, in a seed file.</p>
    <BlogCode label="incident-seed.yaml" code={incidentSeed} copy="copy-blog-rca-seed" />
    <BlogCode label="Start and seed" code={startCmd} copy="copy-blog-rca-cmd" />
    <p class="mt-4"><code>localcloud env</code> exports the SDK endpoints for that runtime, including <code>LOCALCLOUD_GATEWAY</code>, so the commands work whichever ports it was given.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="replay">Replay the payload</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">Copy the shape of the failing message and replace customer values with synthetic ones. Here the upstream service started sending the amount as a decimal string. The script publishes that message and then runs the worker's handling code against it.</p>
    <BlogCode label="replay.py" code={replayPy} copy="copy-blog-rca-replay" />
    <BlogCode label="Output" code={failure} />
    <p class="mt-4">That is the production crash, on your machine, in a second. Run the script again and the same message comes back, because it was never acknowledged. You are now looking at the redelivery loop itself, and you can attach a debugger to it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fix">Fix it and prove it</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">Parse the amount as a decimal and convert to cents:</p>
    <BlogCode label="The fix" code={fixPy} copy="copy-blog-rca-fix" />
    <BlogCode label="Output" code={fixed} />
    <p class="mt-4">The stuck message is processed, the row lands in <code>billing.invoices</code>, and the acknowledgement clears the queue. The local table enforces its schema too: insert a row without <code>invoice_id</code> and the client returns <q>Required destination field invoice_id cannot be NULL</q>, so the next class of bad payload is just as easy to try.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="regression">Keep the replay as a test</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">The seed file and the script are now the incident's regression test. Move them into your integration suite, assert on the inserted row, and run them in CI so this payload can never take the worker down again. Stop the runtime with <code>localcloud stop --data-volume rca-incident-412</code> when you are done. Ship the fix through staging as usual; the difference is that you already know it works.</p>
  </section>
</BlogArticle>
